/-
# Upper composition factors of finitely generated groups (Kourovka Notebook Problem 11.57)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 11.57 (A. Mann, D. Segal): an upper
composition factor of a group `G` is a composition factor of some finite quotient of `G`. Is there
any restriction on the set of non-abelian upper composition factors of a finitely generated group?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.IsSubnormal

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.UpperCompositionFactorsKourovka11Problem57Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 11.57 (A. Mann,
D. Segal). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700749 (`KOU-11.57`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A simple group `T` is a composition factor of a finite group `Q` when it is a homomorphic image of a
subnormal subgroup of `Q` (refining the kernel and the subnormal chain gives a composition series
through it, and conversely). Subnormal is Mathlib's `Subgroup.IsSubnormal`: a finite chain of
subgroups from `H` up to `Q`, each normal in the next (`Subgroup.IsSubnormal.isSubnormal_iff`).
Finite quotients are surjections onto finite groups. A set of non-abelian finite simple groups is a
family `T : ι → Type`, and "exactly" is up to isomorphism. The answer "no restriction" is stated in
the two quantitative forms recorded in the Archive: 63 generators with no abelian upper composition
factors, and 3 generators if abelian ones are allowed.
-/

/-- The simple group `T` is a composition factor of the finite group `Q`: `T` is a homomorphic
image of a subnormal subgroup of `Q`. For simple `T` and finite `Q` this is the same as `T`
occurring as a factor of a composition series of `Q` (refine `ker ≤ H` and the subnormal chain). -/
def IsCompositionFactor (T Q : Type*) [Group T] [Group Q] : Prop :=
  ∃ H : Subgroup Q, H.IsSubnormal ∧ ∃ f : H →* T, Function.Surjective f

/-- `T` is an upper composition factor of `G`: a composition factor of some finite quotient of
`G`. -/
def IsUpperCompositionFactor (T G : Type) [Group T] [Group G] : Prop :=
  ∃ (Q : Type) (_ : Group Q) (_ : Finite Q) (π : G →* Q), Function.Surjective π ∧
    IsCompositionFactor T Q

/-- Kourovka 11.57 (A. Mann, D. Segal), first part of the answer: for every family `(T i)` of
finite non-abelian simple groups there is a group generated by 63 elements whose upper
composition factors are, up to isomorphism, exactly the `T i`. -/
def upperCompositionFactorsAnySet63 : Prop :=
  ∀ (ι : Type) (T : ι → Type) [∀ i, Group (T i)],
    (∀ i, Finite (T i) ∧ IsSimpleGroup (T i) ∧ ∃ a b : T i, a * b ≠ b * a) →
    ∃ (G : Type) (_ : Group G), (∃ s : Fin 63 → G, Subgroup.closure (Set.range s) = ⊤) ∧
      ∀ (Q : Type) [Group Q] [Finite Q], IsSimpleGroup Q →
        (IsUpperCompositionFactor Q G ↔ ∃ i, Nonempty (Q ≃* T i))

/-- Kourovka 11.57 (A. Mann, D. Segal), second part of the answer: for every family `(T i)` of
finite non-abelian simple groups there is a group generated by 3 elements whose non-abelian upper
composition factors are, up to isomorphism, exactly the `T i`. -/
def nonabelianUpperCompositionFactorsAnySet3 : Prop :=
  ∀ (ι : Type) (T : ι → Type) [∀ i, Group (T i)],
    (∀ i, Finite (T i) ∧ IsSimpleGroup (T i) ∧ ∃ a b : T i, a * b ≠ b * a) →
    ∃ (G : Type) (_ : Group G), (∃ s : Fin 3 → G, Subgroup.closure (Set.range s) = ⊤) ∧
      ∀ (Q : Type) [Group Q] [Finite Q], IsSimpleGroup Q → (∃ a b : Q, a * b ≠ b * a) →
        (IsUpperCompositionFactor Q G ↔ ∃ i, Nonempty (Q ≃* T i))

/--
Resolved true: Segal proves that every set of non-abelian finite simple groups is exactly the set of
upper composition factors of some 63-generator group, as recorded in the Kourovka Archive ("There
are no restrictions"). Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group
Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems,
Problem 11.57 (A. Mann, D. Segal); resolution: D. Segal, Proc. London Math. Soc. (3) 82 (2001),
597-613, Kourovka Archive, Problem 11.57: any set of non-abelian finite simple groups is the set of
upper composition factors of a 63-generator group; with abelian upper composition factors allowed, 3
generators suffice, https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
public theorem_wanted upperCompositionFactorsAnySet63_holds : upperCompositionFactorsAnySet63

/--
Resolved true: Segal proves that, allowing abelian upper composition factors, every set of
non-abelian finite simple groups is exactly the set of non-abelian upper composition factors of some
3-generator group. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group
Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems,
Problem 11.57 (A. Mann, D. Segal); resolution: D. Segal, Proc. London Math. Soc. (3) 82 (2001),
597-613, Kourovka Archive, Problem 11.57: any set of non-abelian finite simple groups is the set of
upper composition factors of a 63-generator group; with abelian upper composition factors allowed, 3
generators suffice, https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
public theorem_wanted nonabelianUpperCompositionFactorsAnySet3_holds :
    nonabelianUpperCompositionFactorsAnySet3

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.UpperCompositionFactorsKourovka11Problem57Wanted
